problem_statement:
Convert a small JavaScript to-do application to TypeScript. The application manages a list of tasks with the ability to add, complete, and delete tasks.

JavaScript implementation:

class TodoApp {
  constructor() {
    this.tasks = [];
    this.nextId = 1;
  }

  addTask(title) {
    const task = {
      id: this.nextId++,
      title: title,
      completed: false,
      createdAt: new Date()
    };
    this.tasks.push(task);
    return task;
  }

  completeTask(id) {
    const task = this.tasks.find(t => t.id === id);
    if (task) {
      task.completed = true;
    }
    return task;
  }

  deleteTask(id) {
    const index = this.tasks.findIndex(t => t.id === id);
    if (index !== -1) {
      const deleted = this.tasks.splice(index, 1)[0];
      return deleted;
    }
    return null;
  }

  getAllTasks() {
    return this.tasks;
  }

  getCompletedTasks() {
    return this.tasks.filter(t => t.completed);
  }
}

Convert this application to TypeScript by:
1. Defining a Task interface with appropriate types for id, title, completed, and createdAt.
2. Adding type annotations to the class properties and methods.
3. Adding type annotations to method parameters and return types.
4. Ensuring the class is properly typed for use in a TypeScript environment.

Preserve the original behavior. The application should work exactly as the JavaScript version.
